description:
Wrap existing episode processing functions (_process_episode stages) as Temporal activities for visibility. Keep current queue-based system unchanged - activities will be called by Temporal workflows in parallel.

## Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] activities/episodeIngestion.ts created with all activity functions
- [ ] extractEntitiesActivity wraps entity extraction (graphiti_core.graphiti.extract_entities)
- [ ] deduplicateNodesActivity wraps node deduplication
- [ ] extractEdgesActivity wraps edge extraction
- [ ] resolveEdgesActivity wraps edge resolution
- [ ] saveToGraphActivity wraps graph persistence
- [ ] Each activity has proper error handling (ApplicationFailure.retryable for transient errors)
- [ ] Activities use structured logging (@temporalio/activity log)
- [ ] Timeouts configured appropriately (startToCloseTimeout, scheduleToCloseTimeout)

## Implementation Example

```typescript
// temporal/activities/episodeIngestion.ts
import { ApplicationFailure, log } from '@temporalio/activity';

export async function extractEntitiesActivity(params: {
  episodeUuid: string;
  episodeContent: string;
  episodeType: string;
}): Promise<{ entities: any[]; duration: number }> {
  const startTime = Date.now();

  try {
    log.info('Extracting entities', { episodeUuid: params.episodeUuid });

    // Call existing Python function via HTTP or spawn Python process
    const result = await callPythonFunction('extract_entities', params);

    const duration = Date.now() - startTime;
    log.info('Entity extraction complete', { 
      episodeUuid: params.episodeUuid, 
      entityCount: result.entities.length,
      duration 
    });

    return { entities: result.entities, duration };
  } catch (error: any) {
    // Classify errors
    if (error.message.includes('rate limit') || error.message.includes('timeout')) {
      throw ApplicationFailure.retryable(
        `Entity extraction failed: ${error.message}`,
        'TRANSIENT_ERROR',
        { episodeUuid: params.episodeUuid }
      );
    }

    // Permanent errors (bad input, etc.)
    throw ApplicationFailure.nonRetryable(
      `Invalid episode: ${error.message}`,
      'PERMANENT_ERROR'
    );
  }
}
```

## Notes
- Activities should call existing Python code (via HTTP API or subprocess)
- Don't rewrite Python logic - just wrap it for Temporal visibility
- Use same error classification as current system (TransientError, PermanentError)
- Retry policies should match current system (3 attempts, exponential backoff)

