## Parent Issue
GRAPH-275 / bd-670e2

Create main Temporal workflow that orchestrates episode ingestion using the activities from graphiti-60k. This workflow represents the entire episode processing pipeline with full visibility.

## Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] workflows/ingestEpisode.ts created
- [ ] IngestEpisodeWorkflow calls activities in correct order (extract entities → deduplicate nodes → extract edges → resolve edges → save to graph)
- [ ] Workflow uses deterministic workflow IDs (episode UUID based)
- [ ] Activity proxies configured with appropriate timeouts and retry policies
- [ ] Workflow is idempotent (can replay safely)
- [ ] No I/O or non-deterministic calls in workflow code
- [ ] Workflow execution timeout set (1 hour)
- [ ] Workflow handles activity failures gracefully

## Implementation Example

```typescript
// temporal/workflows/ingestEpisode.ts
import { proxyActivities } from '@temporalio/workflow';
import type * as activities from '../activities/episodeIngestion';

// Configure activity proxies with timeouts and retry policies
const {
  extractEntitiesActivity,
  deduplicateNodesActivity,
  extractEdgesActivity,
  resolveEdgesActivity,
  saveToGraphActivity,
} = proxyActivities<typeof activities>({
  startToCloseTimeout: '5m',      // Max time for single attempt
  scheduleToCloseTimeout: '30m',  // Max total time including retries
  retry: {
    initialInterval: '10s',
    backoffCoefficient: 2,
    maximumAttempts: 3,
    maximumInterval: '300s',       // 5 minutes max
    nonRetryableErrorTypes: ['PERMANENT_ERROR'],
  },
});

export interface IngestEpisodeInput {
  episodeUuid: string;
  episodeContent: string;
  episodeType: string;
  sourceDescription: string;
  createdAt: string;
}

export interface IngestEpisodeResult {
  success: boolean;
  nodesCreated: number;
  edgesCreated: number;
  duration: number;
  error?: string;
}

export async function IngestEpisodeWorkflow(
  input: IngestEpisodeInput
): Promise<IngestEpisodeResult> {
  const startTime = Date.now();

  try {
    // Stage 1: Extract entities
    const { entities } = await extractEntitiesActivity({
      episodeUuid: input.episodeUuid,
      episodeContent: input.episodeContent,
      episodeType: input.episodeType,
    });

    // Stage 2: Deduplicate nodes
    const { deduplicatedNodes } = await deduplicateNodesActivity({
      episodeUuid: input.episodeUuid,
      entities,
    });

    // Stage 3: Extract edges
    const { edges } = await extractEdgesActivity({
      episodeUuid: input.episodeUuid,
      episodeContent: input.episodeContent,
      entities: deduplicatedNodes,
    });

    // Stage 4: Resolve edges
    const { resolvedEdges } = await resolveEdgesActivity({
      episodeUuid: input.episodeUuid,
      edges,
      nodes: deduplicatedNodes,
    });

    // Stage 5: Save to graph
    const { nodesCreated, edgesCreated } = await saveToGraphActivity({
      episodeUuid: input.episodeUuid,
      nodes: deduplicatedNodes,
      edges: resolvedEdges,
    });

    const duration = Date.now() - startTime;

    return {
      success: true,
      nodesCreated,
      edgesCreated,
      duration,
    };
  } catch (error: any) {
    return {
      success: false,
      nodesCreated: 0,
      edgesCreated: 0,
      duration: Date.now() - startTime,
      error: error.message,
    };
  }
}
```

## Notes
- Workflow must be deterministic (no Date.now(), Math.random(), etc. - use Temporal utilities)
- All I/O must be in activities, not in workflow code
- Use episode UUID as workflow ID to prevent duplicates
- Timeout values match current system expectations (~226s average, 300s p95)

